        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): bound userCache growth with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`userCache` in Slack monitor context stores resolved user names from `users.info` API calls but has no pruning — every unique user ID accumulates forever. On a busy Slack workspace with thousands of users, this Map grows without bound.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`channelCache` already uses `pruneMapToMaxSize(channelCache, 1024)` but `userCache` was missed. The fix adds the same pattern at 2048 entries.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents unbounded memory growth in long-running Slack monitor sessions\n- Oldest entries are evicted when the cap is reached\n- No behavioral change for typical usage (2048 entries covers most workspaces)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Before (no pruning)\n```typescript\nuserCache.set(cacheKey, entry);  // ← never removed\n// userCache grows without bound as new users are resolved\n```\n\n### After (bounded at 2048)\n```typescript\nuserCache.set(cacheKey, entry);\npruneMapToMaxSize(userCache, SLACK_USER_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES);  // evicts oldest\n```\n\n### Unit test (10/10 passed)\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.test.ts\n\n ✓ evicts the oldest user name when the bounded user cache fills (new test)\n ✓ ... (9 existing tests)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\n### Lint + Format\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts  # No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts              # Correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts: +2 lines (SLACK_USER_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES + pruneMapToMaxSize)\n- extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.test.ts: +15 lines (eviction test)\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
